  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY NIGHT THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 200 AM CDT Mon Aug 10 2026\n\nHot conditions continue with decreasing rain chances: Ensembles \nsuggest that the upper ridge will slide further east and become \ncentered just south of the area by mid week. This will allow a \nmore westerly component at 850mb with some of the highest temps\nadvecting in (850mb temps of 24-26C). Latest NBM continues to \nshow widespread upper 90s to lower 100s mainly across locations \nwest of Highway 65 on Wednesday. Locations that have seen \nrain recently may still be too green to reach 100 but it will \nbe close as consecutive days of these high temps will begin to \ndry soils/grass out. Dewpoints will mix out a little further in\nthe afternoon each day however the higher air temps may still \nbalance out to allow for continued heat indicies of 100-108. \n\nLatest ensemble guidance has trended stronger with the upper\nridge and would lead to hotter and drier conditions for \nThursday through at least Friday. It is not unusual for these \nstronger summertime highs to remain established for longer \nperiods of time than deterministic models originally indicate. \nWe are becoming more confident that heat headlines may need to \nbe extended into Thursday and perhaps Friday however will need \nto see how much mixing occurs and the exact placement of rain\nchances to our north. Highs may end of remaining well into the \n90s to around 100 Thursday and Friday for the southwest half of \nthe area. Rain chances have shifted further north for Thursday \nand Friday and this trend may continue further into the weekend.\nLatest CPC guidance indicates the prolonged heat may last or \nredevelop over the area during the following week (August 17-21).\nTherefore heat sensitive groups will need to prepare for the \npotential of an extended period of heat with low rain chances.",
